-- REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 (2026-10-26, session rem-a1, pillar research; agent_issues 100211, 100408, 1000031, 100456, 1000002, 1000316, 1000317, 100625, 1000012).
-- Nine issues of the research cluster stay open because their definitions of done are outcome-bound (a window, a budget day, a first publish) or wait for a code task another session holds. Each gets a dated note that names the measured
-- numbers, the date its probe can first pass and the doer, so that the state is a record on the issue and not only a line in a report. Two follow-ups that the session wrote down become issues with a closing probe and a doer:
-- TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1 (the generic RESEARCH-TERMINAL closing probe) and NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1 (the stale-retraction age as a registry metric, issue 1000012 defect A part 3). No status, priority or probe of an existing issue changes.
-- Rows written: agent_issues 9 notes (appended once, the marker stops a second run) and 2 inserts, remediation_contracts 1 (upsert on the new metric issue), decision_log 1. No DELETE, no DROP.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE agent_issues SET description = substr(description, 1, instr(description, char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') - 1) WHERE id IN (100211, 100408, 1000031, 100456, 1000002, 1000316, 1000317, 100625, 1000012) AND instr(description, char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') > 0;
-- Rollback note: the two inserted issues are not deleted on rollback (no silent drop, doctrine section 6); close them through issue_triage with evidence or supersede them.

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): gpt-oss-120b took 252,692 of the 290,494 research-exec neurons of 2026-10-26 (87 percent), but every one of them was spent before the daily budget hold at 04:11Z; RESEARCH-COST-FIRST-1 (0.36.0, glm-5.3-flash first) merged at 09:42Z and the model-order event shows it live on every tick. 2026-10-27 is the first day under the new order and the probe reads yesterday, so it can first pass on 2026-10-28 and a second pass closes it. If gpt-oss-120b is still over half of 2026-10-27, the next lever is the per-stage model lists (review, revise and verify made 260 of its 344 calls on 2026-10-26). Doer: qnfo-research-exec.'
WHERE id = 100211 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): research-exec plus errata-hub neurons by day are 4,243,641 on 10-19, 3,616,982 on 10-20 and 1,753,306 on 10-21 (all over 600,000), then 322,110 to 416,435 on 10-22 to 10-25 and 402,031 so far on 10-26. The probe holds those three days in its 7-day window until 2026-10-28, so with 10-26 to 10-28 at or under 600,000 it first passes on 2026-10-29; the 36 papers published on 10-22 to 10-26 clear its 14-paper floor. There is nothing to change for the window: the daily research budget (research_daily_neurons 360000) holds the day total. The ticket closes by the probe, on its second pass.'
WHERE id = 100408 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): the STILL_DEFECTIVE reading has two parts that waiting does not fix. workers_ai_cost_30d_usd (300.74) is a 30-day figure that carries 10-17 to 10-21 (1.27M to 4.24M neurons a day). research_neurons_per_publication_7d (46,737.5; research-exec plus errata-hub plus paper-reviser over the 7 complete days, divided by papers published) averaged about 50,000 neurons a paper on 10-22 to 10-26 (1.81M neurons, 36 papers), and errata-hub took 64,910 to 182,577 neurons a day in that span (111,537 on 10-26) for confirm and respond work whose last step, the corrective research row, is never claimed (code tasks ct_im1000472 RESEARCH-ERRATA-CLAIM-1 and ct_im1000475 CLAIM-ERRATA-SHARE-1, both queued in the code loop on qnfo-research-exec/worker.js). Levers in order: get the errata rows claimed so that the spend yields published corrections; the cost-first order of issue 100211 (first full day 2026-10-27).'
WHERE id = 1000031 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): after CONTENT-PIPELINE-MEASURE-1 (the view no longer counts an erratum twice or a closed row) and ERRATA-REMEDIATION-MERGE-1 (one open errata remediation row per paper) the count reads 1032. What remains is capacity: 154 queued errata remediation rows (151 of them in the 192-row ready window) and 87 wontfix, none ever claimed or published. The doers are code tasks ct_im1000475 (CLAIM-ERRATA-SHARE-1, claimNew order; attempts 2, last error noop-proposal) and ct_im1000472 (RESEARCH-ERRATA-CLAIM-1), queued behind the code loop''s file claim on qnfo-research-exec/worker.js (to 21:36Z), and RB-ERRATA-SHARE-1 in qnfo-fleet-control. Closing probe unchanged: content_items_over_stage_sla = 0.'
WHERE id = 100456 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): the chain has its producer for errata_actions: routeHighRiskErrata routes high-risk errata one remediation row per paper (243 rows routed) and verifyRoutedErrata marks a routed row verified when its remediation row publishes (qnfo-research-exec 0.37.0 and 0.38.0). The probe reads errata_queue internal-open 572 (needs under 50; the confirm tick settles at most errata_confirm_max = 12 an hour), errata_actions verified 1 (a row of 2026-10-02; the new path has verified none because no errata remediation row has been claimed yet) and notes_publish_queue 0 (the notes queue; this session left that clause as written). Doers: ct_im1000475 and ct_im1000472 for the claim, the hourly confirm cap for the backlog.'
WHERE id = 1000002 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): /repo-ledger reads healthy:false with consolidated_ok 0 and by_status empty because research_run_ledger holds no row: no paper has been published since 0.35.0 merged (07:52Z), the daily research budget having been spent at 04:11Z (8 papers published before it). The first publish after the 00:00Z budget reset writes the first deposit; three ok deposits and no failure close the issue. Doer: qnfo-research-exec (publish stage; repoSyncTick every 10 minutes retries failed deposits and reported sync ok at 19:41Z).'
WHERE id = 1000316 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:00Z): the code is done on main: qnfo-cloud-ops 1.37.0 (07:48Z) and qnfo-research-exec 0.35.1 with errata-hub 1.8.2 (09:35Z) set change_actor on every papers write that touches a column the ledger tracks (13 of the 16 UPDATE papers sites in research-exec; the other 3 write doi_flagged or release_gate_* only, which the ledger does not record). The ledger holds 0 unattributed rows after 07:21:28Z. The probe fails only on 252 unattributed status changes between 07:20:56Z and 07:21:28Z (the gate restore before 1.37.0), which leave its 24-hour window at 07:22Z on 2026-10-27; it first passes then and a second pass closes it. Caveat: no research-exec write has reached the ledger since 09:35Z (no publishing), so those sites are unproven in production until the first publish.'
WHERE id = 1000317 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:05Z): the probe (RESEARCH-CLUSTER-CLOSEOUTS-2) reads 0 orphans and 1 live row above the re-arm ceiling: ac9cce13-f637-4a7f-abbe-7a02e5e2d884, status deferred, terminal_rearms 5, re-armed before PARK-REARM-CAP-1 (0.36.7). It passes when that row publishes or when the cap parks it at its next terminal. Doer: qnfo-research-exec (claimNew and the backpressure tick decide when it runs).'
WHERE id = 100625 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26 (read 20:05Z): defect B (the write-only mirror) is fixed by MIRROR-DRIFT-1 (0.38.0): the ticks at 19:31Z, 19:41Z, 19:51Z and 20:01Z each checked 20 papers, found 14 to 18 drifted, repaired 10 (the per-tick cap) and had no error; a full pass over the 704 published papers takes about 36 ticks (six hours), and the repair cap means a second pass catches the remainder. Defect A (1) and the breach in (3) are noticeRepairEscalate (0.38.1): an owner paper retracted for 24 hours with a backup present files one NOTICE-REPAIR-STUCK-1 issue with a closing contract (none is filed today: all 28 retracted papers carry a qnf- identifier and belong to the claim sweep). (2), the bounded retry, was already rlDbRun. A registry metric for the age in (3) is the issue NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1. The closing probe is the code-read marker NOTICE-REPAIR-ESCALATE-1, which the consumer could not see until its checkout moved past 0.38.1.'
WHERE id = 1000012 AND instr(COALESCE(description, ''), 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1 2026-10-26') = 0;

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1: the generic closing probe of a RESEARCH-TERMINAL issue does not resolve a row parked with PARKED-POISON-1 or an archived rem- row, so its issue never closes', 'Charter pillar: research. Found 2026-10-26 by session rem-a1 while closing RESEARCH-TERMINAL issues: qnfo-research-exec terminalResolveProbe(id, kind) resolves an issue only when the row has left wontfix and the parked stage, or is parked with terminal_rearms at or above TERMINAL_RECOVERY_MAX (2) while the pipeline moves, or (kinds hard-review and mismatch) is parked with that reason while the pipeline moves. A row parked with PARKED-POISON-1 for any other reason, or an archived rem- row, matches none of them, so the issues that were closed in migrations/2026-10-26-research-cluster-closeouts.sql needed a probe of their own, and the next RESEARCH-TERMINAL issue for such a row will stay open. Change: terminalResolveProbe counts a row with status wontfix and an error that starts with PARKED-POISON-1, or an archived rem- row, as resolved (marker TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1 in a comment above the function), in the same change as migrations/research-terminal-rearmed.test.mjs, which pins the function to the SQL of the 2026-10-20 migration (a worker-only change fails that suite), plus a migration that rewrites the generic contract text of the open RESEARCH-TERMINAL issues. A change to worker.js and a test file cannot be done as a one-file code task, so the doer is a session. Definition of done: the marker is in qnfo-research-exec/worker.js and node migrations/research-terminal-rearmed.test.mjs passes.
code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-research-exec/worker.js"], "contains": "TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1"}', 'session-rem-a1', 'reliability', 'low', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues x WHERE x.title = 'TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1: the generic closing probe of a RESEARCH-TERMINAL issue does not resolve a row parked with PARKED-POISON-1 or an archived rem- row, so its issue never closes' AND x.status = 'open');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1: register the age of the oldest retracted owner paper that has a full backup as a metric with a trigger (agent_issues 1000012, defect A part 3)', 'Charter pillar: autonomy. Issue 1000012 defect A asks for a stale-retraction age metric, so that an owner paper retracted for more than 24 hours with a full backup present is a breach. noticeRepairEscalate (qnfo-research-exec 0.38.1) files a NOTICE-REPAIR-STUCK-1 issue for each such paper, which makes the breach visible and owned, but metric_registry has no row that measures it, so metrics_in_breach does not count it. Change: register a metric (suggested key owner_papers_retracted_over_24h, target 0, owner qnfo-research-exec) that counts living-paper papers with status retracted, no qnf- identifier and no research_queue row, whose earliest paper_integrity_backups row in qnfo-audit is more than 24 hours old, together with its trigger in analytics_metric_triggers (threshold, lever, definition of done), as CLAUDE.md requires for a new metric. Doer: qnfo-fleet-control (metric refresh and triggers) with a session for the migration. Definition of done: the metric row exists in metric_registry and has a trigger. The contract of this issue reads metric_registry.', 'session-rem-a1', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues x WHERE x.title = 'NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1: register the age of the oldest retracted owner paper that has a full backup as a metric with a trigger (agent_issues 1000012, defect A part 3)' AND x.status = 'open');

INSERT INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, next_due_at)
SELECT 'issue-' || a.id, a.id, 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1: the stale-retraction age of owner papers (1000012 defect A part 3) is a registry metric with a trigger', 'qnfo-fleet-control and a session register the metric, its refresh and its trigger; this contract closes the issue when the metric row exists', 'SELECT ''1'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''owner_papers_retracted_over_24h'') AS TEXT) AS observed', 'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', datetime('now')
FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.title = 'NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1: register the age of the oldest retracted owner paper that has a full backup as a metric with a trigger (agent_issues 1000012, defect A part 3)' AND a.status = 'open' ORDER BY a.id DESC LIMIT 1
ON CONFLICT (class) DO UPDATE SET issue_id = excluded.issue_id, precondition = excluded.precondition, action = excluded.action, verify_probe = excluded.verify_probe, verify_transport = excluded.verify_transport, escalate_to = excluded.escalate_to, max_attempts = excluded.max_attempts, expected_cadence_h = excluded.expected_cadence_h, status = 'active', last_verdict = NULL, last_attempt_at = NULL, attempts = 0, next_due_at = datetime('now');

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session-rem-a1', 'an open issue is only as good as the record on it: the owner, the date its probe can first pass and the blocker belong on the issue, and a follow-up that exists only in a report is lost (OWNER-NO-LOOSE-ENDS-1)', 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1: dated hand-off notes on nine open research-cluster issues; two follow-up issues (TERMINAL-RESOLVE-PARKED-POISON-1, NOTICE-REPAIR-STALE-METRIC-1) with a closing probe and a doer', 'agent_issues, ai_call_counters, research_queue, paper_change_ledger, code_tasks and /work-locks read on 2026-10-26 19:45Z to 20:05Z: 100211 gpt-oss-120b 87 percent of 290,494 neurons before the 04:11Z hold; 100408 three days over 600,000 leave the window on 10-28; 1000317 252 unattributed rows at 07:20:56Z to 07:21:28Z, none since; 100456 154 queued and 87 wontfix errata rows, none claimed; 1000316 research_run_ledger empty', 'applied by migration', 'agent_issues.description of nine issues (appended text), two new issues, one remediation_contracts row; no status, priority, probe or contract of an existing issue changes', 'the Rollback line of migrations/2026-10-26-rem-a1-handoff.sql strips the nine notes; the two issues are closed through issue_triage with evidence', 'the state of the research cluster is a record on each issue with its owner and its first-pass date', 'each issue''s contract reads the same on the next tick; the two new issues are open with a probe and a doer', 'research: the next session reads the blocker and the date on the issue instead of rediscovering them', 'the offline suite replays the file on node:sqlite (notes appended once, replay a no-op, Rollback restores every description, the metric contract flips when the row exists)'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log x WHERE x.action LIKE 'REM-A1-HANDOFF-1:%');
